Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 06:35:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 028/154] fix: suppress the chrome-layer context menu where it
 is SHOWN, not built
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The InitMenu guard emptied Chromium's own menu model, which stopped the crash -
but the menu still appeared. macOS contributes Look Up, Speech, Writing Tools
and Services for a text selection independently of Chromium's model, so what
was left was a menu containing only the system items and none of ours.

ChromeWebContentsViewDelegateViewsMac::ShowContextMenu now returns before
building anything when the WebContents is on the system profile - which is
where Atrium's chrome layer lives. Nothing is built, so nothing is shown.

The InitMenu guard stays as defence in depth: it covers any other path that
constructs this menu without going through the Mac view delegate.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 ...me_web_contents_view_delegate_views_mac.mm | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tab_contents/chrome_web_contents_view_delegate_views_mac.mm b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tab_contents/chrome_web_contents_view_delegate_views_mac.mm
index 564c8c000c5be..570dc0fffced3 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tab_contents/chrome_web_contents_view_delegate_views_mac.mm
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tab_contents/chrome_web_contents_view_delegate_views_mac.mm
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <optional>
 
 #import "chrome/browser/renderer_host/chrome_render_widget_host_view_mac_delegate.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/profiles/profile.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/browser_window/public/browser_window_interface.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/browser_window/public/global_browser_collection.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/cocoa/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu_mac_cocoa.h"
@@ -70,6 +71,27 @@ ChromeWebContentsViewDelegateViewsMac::GetDragDestDelegate() {
 void ChromeWebContentsViewDelegateViewsMac::ShowContextMenu(
     content::RenderFrameHost& render_frame_host,
     const content::ContextMenuParams& params) {
+  // ATRIUM: top chrome gets no context menu at all.
+  //
+  // Atrium's chrome layer - sidebar, pill, foyer - is WebUI on the SYSTEM
+  // profile (AtriumChromeContext uses ProfileManager::GetSystemProfilePath),
+  // and a page menu there crashed the browser: it dereferences profile-keyed
+  // services no system profile has.
+  //
+  // Suppressed HERE rather than only in RenderViewContextMenu::InitMenu
+  // because that empties Chromium's own model while macOS still contributes
+  // Look Up / Speech / Writing Tools / Services for a text selection - so the
+  // menu still appeared, just with nothing of ours in it. Returning before the
+  // menu is built is what stops it showing.
+  //
+  // These surfaces build their own DOM menus (sidebar-menu.js), and
+  // no page content is hosted on the system profile in this browser.
+  Profile* const profile =
+      Profile::FromBrowserContext(web_contents_->GetBrowserContext());
+  if (profile && profile->IsSystemProfile()) {
+    return;
+  }
+
   BuildMenuAsync(
       render_frame_host, params,
       base::BindOnce(&ChromeWebContentsViewDelegateViewsMac::ShowMenu,
